From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 04:53:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: the PS4's GPU through Mesa's RADV, after Eden4

Eden's Vulkan renderer on the PS4, as Eden4 (github.com/xatyy/eden4, GPL-3.0-or-later, built on
this same Eden commit) does it: RADV linked into the executable (its ICD entry point installed
as vkGetInstanceProcAddr, no loader), an Orbis window system without a surface, a swapchain of
three linear images registered with VideoOut whose flips are queued behind the GPU's work
(vk_swapchain_ps4.cpp, from Eden4), and GPU memory sized from the free direct memory left after
the Switch's 4 GiB: smaller VMA blocks, texture and buffer cache budgets from it, staging buffers
capped at 64 MiB, and a reclaim (wait for the GPU, free idle staging buffers, retry) when an
allocation would leave too little or fails. common/ps4_diagnostics.h is Eden4's.

Not yet built for the PS4 or run on a console.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VdsH7DVAudgDzMpBqJZHAz
